From 57a758e06c73b8d668d01ba46b732315f52104cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:48:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] refactor(chat): move provider helpers, usage logging
 and model resolution out of proxy_service
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

First step of the stream_chat split (Phase 4.1). Three verbatim moves, no
behaviour change:

- app/services/provider_utils.py — the pure helpers every provider-facing
  path shares: LiteLLM kwargs, usage extraction from chunks/wrappers/
  responses, prompt text, provider error formatting and the read-timeout
  retry rule, SSE delta/error frames, chunk serialisation, token-cost
  quote, upstream stream close. Public names; the underscored names stay
  as aliases and proxy_service re-exports them for existing importers and
  test patch targets.
- app/services/usage_logging_service.py — `log_usage` (the single write
  path every billed operation ends in), `_apply_cost_to_user`,
  `reserve_auxiliary_llm_usage`, `settle_auxiliary_usage`.
- app/services/model_resolution_service.py — `resolve_model_and_key`,
  `assert_model_supports_text_chat`.

speech/video/image billing, metered usage, transcription, chat title,
image prompt, chat tools and both memory extractors now import from the
new modules; the four lazy `from app.services.proxy_service import ...`
inside function bodies that hid the cycle are gone. proxy_service shrinks
from 2777 to 2166 lines.

Verified: 1371 tests, mypy baseline unchanged, vulture clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UTnpHajSmkk2JMLfuQoV7o
